    "created_at": "2016-06-28T16:08:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-06-28T16:08:39Z",
    "body": "Yep, that would do nicely. Alternately you could restructure it as an algorithm with steps, e.g.\n1. If this element's href content attribute is absent, set this element's url to null.\n2. Parse this element's href content attribute value relative to this element's node document. If parsing is successful, set this element's url to the result; otherwise, set this element's url to null.\n\nThanks for being willing to work on this, @WillRay!\n",
